## Toolchain (mise)

Tooling is pinned in [`mise.toml`](mise.toml). `tooling/` is a **git submodule** sourced from
[Project-Zomboid-Template](https://github.com/codyduong/Project-Zomboid-Template) — it holds
the actual scripts; `mise.toml` here is a thin per-repo shim over them. One-time: install
[mise](https://mise.jdx.dev), then:

```
git submodule update --init
mise install
mise tasks
```

| Task | What it does |
|------|--------------|
| `mise run check` | luafmt + emmylua_check |
| `mise run decompile <version>` | Decompile the installed game into `.decompiled/<version>/` |
| `mise run bump <version>` | Set `modversion` in every `mod.info` |
| `mise run package <tag>` | Validate versions + assemble `dist/__MOD_NAME__` |
| `mise run deploy <client\|server\|all>` | Package + sync for in-game testing |
| `mise run testhost [--reset]` | Ephemeral local dedicated server for MP testing |
| `mise run publish <test\|prod> "note"` | Upload to Steam Workshop via steamcmd |
| `mise run sync-template` | Pull the latest `tooling/` (Project-Zomboid-Template) commit |

**Keeping in sync with the template**: `mise run sync-template` updates `tooling/` to the
template's current tip and stages the submodule bump — review the diff, then commit. To pin
and skip an update, just don't run it. To fully diverge (vendor `tooling/` permanently and
drop the submodule link): `git submodule deinit tooling && git rm tooling`, then copy the
scripts in directly and edit freely — see the template's
[docs/USING-THIS-TEMPLATE.md](https://github.com/codyduong/Project-Zomboid-Template/blob/main/docs/USING-THIS-TEMPLATE.md).

**Secrets / local overrides:** `cp mise.local.toml.example mise.local.toml` and set
`STEAM_USERNAME` + `STEAM_PASSWORD`. `mise.local.toml` is git-ignored.

